From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 20:43:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: avd: read frame-based HEVC pictures by
 default

hevc_frame_parse was added off by default so the slice header reader
could be proven before it ran for everyone. It now has been:

- its slice fields, header bytes, sizes and entry points match a
  userspace reference that sends SLICE_PARAMS on every picture of the
  HEVC Main and Main 10 test streams (54 of 54);
- with it on, Chromium's frame-based V4L2 HEVC decoder plays HEVC Main
  and Main 10 on the AVD with no dropped frames, and the displayed
  pictures match an independent reference decode as closely as the 8-bit
  H.264 and AV1 paths do;
- requests that carry slice parameters (VA-API) take the existing path
  either way; their decoded frames stay identical to software.

Off, a frame-based client gets every HEVC picture refused and falls back
to software decoding. Make the reader the default. The parameter stays
writable so it can still be turned off at run time.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c
index cfb847dbec..14954a3209 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/avd/avd-hevc.c
@@ -24,12 +24,12 @@
  * Chromium sends each HEVC picture as Annex-B NAL units with no slice
  * parameters (frame-based decoding). With this set the slice headers are read
  * from the picture; without it such a picture is refused before it reaches the
- * hardware.
+ * hardware. Requests that carry slice parameters (VA-API) never use it.
  */
-static bool hevc_frame_parse;
+static bool hevc_frame_parse = true;
 module_param(hevc_frame_parse, bool, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(hevc_frame_parse,
-		 "Read HEVC slice headers from Annex-B pictures sent without slice parameters (default: off)");
+		 "Read HEVC slice headers from Annex-B pictures sent without slice parameters (default: on)");
 
 bool avd_hevc_frame_parse_enabled(void)
 {
